Trials HD port: changes to the ReXGlue SDK (applied to the pinned submodule
commit by CMake at configure time; regenerate with tools/export_sdk_patch.sh).

- input/mnk: synthesize XamInputGetKeystroke events from bound keys (the
  game's menus read keystrokes)
- vulkan command processor: host presentation FPS cap (present_fps_limit),
  bypassed when the game loop already paces real frames (present_fps_limit_guest_paced),
  guest FPS / draws / resolves per frame logging (log_guest_fps)
- core: unlink the guest memory shm right after creating it (no leaks on crash)
- vulkan presenter: VK_EXT_headless_surface (vulkan_headless_surface)
- graphics: per-occlusion-query and per-frame present logs moved to trace
- resolve shaders: pack 16_16 / 16_16_16_16 destinations in the copy's number
  format (signed integer depth for shadow maps) - sources in
  src/graphics/shaders/xesl, rebuilt with tools/build_resolve_shaders.sh
- SPIR-V texture fetch: result exponent bias from fetch constant word 3 (was
  word 4, the LOD bias), integer number format for 16-bit textures
- resolve readback: readback_resolve_max_bytes (read back only small resolves)
- render targets: elide_rt_transfers (ownership transfers of resolve-cleared
  ranges become clears; transfers fully overwritten by Direct3D 9 clear
  rectangles are dropped), execute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu on by default
- input: serialize InputSystem (device list rebuilt concurrently by several
  guest threads - heap corruption)
- graphics: lock the command processor's CallInThread queue (pushed from
  other threads); logging: reserve the category registry (read lock-free)
- storage & paths: default user data directory next to executable (self-contained); config_path() getter
- macOS: Apple Silicon presentation defaults
- ui/overlay: achievements close callback and input gating
- command processor CPU: sequential register writes (type-0 packets) go
  through the range path, context registers (0x2000-0x3FFF) are bulk-copied,
  the unknown-register debug check is a bit test instead of a big switch, the
  memexport readback cvar lookup only runs for memexport draws, and
  SharedMemory::RequestRanges reuses its scratch vector (720p uncapped on an
  RX 6600: ~145 -> ~183 FPS, now GPU-bound)
- vulkan: skip draws with no observable effect (no pixel shader output,
  depth, stencil, memexport or occlusion query: ~170 per frame in Trials HD),
  counted in the log_guest_fps line
- command processor idle: shorter spin before waiting for new commands, and
  WAIT_REG_MEM naps after a short spin instead of yielding for the whole wait
- threading: event-driven WaitMultiple (sleeps until a condition changes
  instead of polling every millisecond and spinning near each timeout)
- vulkan presenter: remember the swapchain format of the final guest output
  paint pipeline (the format check failed on every paint, so each paint
  awaited the previous one on the GPU behind the queued guest frames and
  recreated the pipeline - GPU-bound, only every other frame was presented:
  2560x1440 on an RX 7800 XT, 169 FPS rendered but 85 presented -> 169);
  presented frames are counted (Presenter::presented_frame_count) and shown
  as "presented fps" on the log_guest_fps line
- ui: dialogs say whether they need continuous repaint; the always-present
  achievement toast only does while showing one (the window was repainted
  ~1400 times per second with VSync off)
- web (Emscripten) memory model (docs/web-port/README.md 7.9.2-7.9.3, W-L04):
  one guest window with the aliases folded per heap, page protection as
  bookkeeping, dirty-bitmap write tracking delivered to the invalidation
  callbacks (memory_emscripten.cpp, exception_handler_emscripten.cpp and
  REX_PLATFORM_EMSCRIPTEN / REX_ARCH_WASM branches; native code unchanged)
- web (Emscripten) platform layer (W-L15): POSIX files accept the web, with
  branches for the clock (CLOCK_MONOTONIC), thread ids/names/affinity and APC
  wakeups; fiber_emscripten.cpp; web UI loop, window and main(); linked-in GPU
  plugins (RegisterStaticGpuPlugin); weak kernel stubs so a game's exports
  override them in a static link; console logging; xxHash/RenderDoc/
  disruptorplus portability (all guarded; native code unchanged)

diff --git a/include/rex/audio/web/web_audio_driver.h b/include/rex/audio/web/web_audio_driver.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ca49f59
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/rex/audio/web/web_audio_driver.h
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+/**
+ * @file        audio/web/web_audio_driver.h
+ * @brief       Audio output of the web (Emscripten) build: a shared-memory ring
+ *              read by the page's AudioWorklet
+ *
+ * The drivers' frames (6-channel big-endian) are mixed to interleaved stereo
+ * and written into WebAudioRing, which lives in the wasm memory (a
+ * SharedArrayBuffer); the page's AudioWorklet (web/audio_worklet.js in Trials
+ * HD Recompiled) plays from it. The ring's fill paces the guest like the SDL
+ * device callback does natively: one client-semaphore release per frame
+ * mixed. While nothing plays the ring (no user gesture yet, a suspended
+ * AudioContext), frames are dropped at the playback rate instead so the
+ * game's audio threads keep their normal speed.
+ */
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <rex/platform.h>
+
+#if !REX_PLATFORM_EMSCRIPTEN
+#error "rex/audio/web/web_audio_driver.h is for the web (Emscripten) build only"
+#endif
+
+#include <atomic>
+#include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <deque>
+#include <mutex>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include <rex/audio/audio_driver.h>
+#include <rex/thread.h>
+
+namespace rex::audio::web {
+
+// Shared with web/audio_worklet.js; little-endian, offsets fixed.
+struct WebAudioRing {
+  static constexpr uint32_t kCapacityFrames = 8192;
+  static constexpr uint32_t kChannels = 2;
+
+  std::atomic<uint32_t> write_frame;  // 0: frames written in total (producer)
+  std::atomic<uint32_t> read_frame;   // 4: frames read in total (worklet)
+  uint32_t capacity_frames;           // 8
+  uint32_t sample_rate;               // 12
+  uint32_t channels;                  // 16
+  std::atomic<uint32_t> underruns;    // 20: worklet: quanta short of data while being fed
+  std::atomic<uint32_t> heartbeat;   // 24: worklet: +1 per render quantum while running
+  std::atomic<uint32_t> peak_milli;   // 28: worklet: max |sample| * 1000 played
+  float samples[kCapacityFrames * kChannels];  // 32: interleaved L R
+};
+static_assert(offsetof(WebAudioRing, samples) == 32);
+
+// The one ring (static storage, so inside the initial wasm memory).
+WebAudioRing& GetWebAudioRing();
+
+// One guest audio client. The game opens several (music, effects, ...);
+// natively the OS mixes their streams, here one mixer thread does: each
+// playback period it takes one queued frame from every client, sums them into
+// the ring and releases each of those clients' semaphores.
+class WebAudioDriver : public AudioDriver {
+ public:
+  WebAudioDriver(memory::Memory* memory, rex::thread::Semaphore* semaphore);
+  ~WebAudioDriver() override;
+
+  void SubmitFrame(uint32_t frame_ptr) override;
+
+  static constexpr uint32_t kFrameRate = 48000;
+  static constexpr uint32_t kGuestChannels = 6;
+  static constexpr uint32_t kChannelSamples = 256;
+  static constexpr uint32_t kFrameSamples = kGuestChannels * kChannelSamples;
+
+  // Mixer thread: adds this client's oldest queued frame (as stereo) to
+  // `mix` and releases its semaphore; false when nothing is queued.
+  bool MixFrame(float* mix, bool to_output);
+
+ private:
+  rex::thread::Semaphore* semaphore_;
+  std::mutex frames_mutex_;
+  std::deque<std::vector<float>> frames_queued_;
+  std::vector<std::vector<float>> frames_unused_;
+};
+
+}  // namespace rex::audio::web
